/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.idea/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Raw datasets are COMMITTED, on purpose.
#
# admet.data.loaders caches them here on first run, so a clone that skips
# this would still work - but only while the MoleculeNet URLs stay up and
# serve the same bytes. Committing them means every teammate trains on the
# same file, a changed upstream distribution shows up as a diff instead of
# as an unexplained change in the numbers, and the project runs offline.
# They are small: 123 KB for Tox21, 20 KB for ClinTox.
#
# Anything else that lands here is a scratch download and stays ignored.
/data/*
!/data/tox21.csv.gz
!/data/clintox.csv.gz

# Run outputs are COMMITTED too, so results are readable without rerunning
# 3.83 h of training. The per-run JSON is the provenance for every number in
# the CSVs - it carries the config, the seed, the split sizes, every tuning
# trial, the library versions and the git commit - so committing the tables
# without it would leave the summary unverifiable.
#
# Regenerate with `make aggregate && make plots`; see README > Findings.
#
# No .gitkeep placeholders: both directories hold committed content, so they
# exist in a clone on their own.
